From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SplitPlay <splitplay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] splitplay: leave the NVIDIA driver settings to the service

The workers changed one shared driver database (DRS) each: the "SplitPlay
worker" application profile (PREFERRED_PSTATE = PREFER_MAX) and the global
OGL_CPL_PREFER_DXPRESENT on the base profile, at start-up, again at every
stream start, and the global value back when they exited. With several
desks the workers raced on create and save, and the first worker to exit
restored the global value while other desks were still streaming.

The SplitPlay service now owns these settings (NvAPI DRS from the
service, one writer, its own record of the previous values): it applies
them before every worker start and restores them when it stops and on
uninstall. The worker no longer touches them:

- no nvprefs at start-up, at stream start (streaming_will_start) or at
  exit;
- `--restore-nvprefs-undo` is kept: it restores the global value from an
  undo file left by a worker from before this change and deletes the
  application profile (patch 0015).

nvenc_latency_over_power and nvenc_opengl_vulkan_on_dxgi no longer do
anything in the worker; the service's host settings decide instead.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01J21Rm2K11gCVojFauZ8YWQ

diff --git a/src/main.cpp b/src/main.cpp
index ccb5f01a0421fc61f04b583dd5e0f2febffc8510..a6a4102d08c892203b7b961fe1f0c4a818566810 100644
--- a/src/main.cpp
+++ b/src/main.cpp
@@ -278,17 +278,10 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[]) {
   }
 
 #ifdef _WIN32
-  // Modify relevant NVIDIA control panel settings if the system has corresponding gpu
-  if (nvprefs_instance.load()) {
-    // Restore global settings to the undo file left by improper termination of sunshine.exe
-    nvprefs_instance.restore_from_and_delete_undo_file_if_exists();
-    // Modify application settings for sunshine.exe
-    nvprefs_instance.modify_application_profile();
-    // Modify global settings, undo file is produced in the process to restore after improper termination
-    nvprefs_instance.modify_global_profile();
-    // Unload dynamic library to survive driver re-installation
-    nvprefs_instance.unload();
-  }
+  // SplitPlay: the NVIDIA driver settings (the worker's "prefer maximum performance" application profile and the
+  // global Vulkan/OpenGL present method) belong to the SplitPlay service, which applies them once for every desk and
+  // restores them; several workers changing one driver database at once raced. `--restore-nvprefs-undo` still
+  // cleans up what workers before this change left behind.
 
   // Wait as long as possible to terminate Sunshine.exe during logoff/shutdown
   SetProcessShutdownParameters(0x100, SHUTDOWN_NORETRY);
@@ -519,11 +512,7 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[]) {
   task_pool.join();
 
 #ifdef _WIN32
-  // Restore global NVIDIA control panel settings
-  if (nvprefs_instance.owning_undo_file() && nvprefs_instance.load()) {
-    nvprefs_instance.restore_global_profile();
-    nvprefs_instance.unload();
-  }
+  // SplitPlay: nothing to restore, the service owns the NVIDIA driver settings (see above).
 #endif
 
   return lifetime::desired_exit_code;
diff --git a/src/platform/windows/misc.cpp b/src/platform/windows/misc.cpp
